ete the clause there.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhCanvasTool.Outline.cs"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T021638Z-269e1e06", "fid": "R-14"}, "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-17: a wire the reader cannot place on a free parameter is counted twice", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The fix is in place and R-17 is recorded fixed. One inexactness in the count it now shows the caller: for a parameter object with an input grip, ReadFullNode calls ReadPort on the same parameter twice, once for its input port and once for its output port (src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/CanvasReader.cs:202-204), and each call walks the same `Sources` and adds to `dropped`. A source it cannot place there adds 2 to `UnreadWires`, so `unread` can read '2 wire(s) could not be read' for one wire. The statement still appears, which is what R-17 asked for; only the number is high. Default: ACCEPT. Fixing it touches a judgeable file and buys a review round.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/CanvasReader.cs"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T021638Z-269e1e06", "fid": "R-17"}, "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-18: the group refusal has no unit test; VRF-019 step 22 is its only evidence", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The class is closed by construction and R-18 is recorded fixed: the default lookup refuses a group, and only TryGetUnprotectedObject and ResolveIds(acceptGroups: true) return one. The decision (`obj is GH_Group`) and its text (ToolHelpers.GroupRefusal) sit in the host-coupled ToolHelpers.cs, so no test in Cordyceps.Tests exercises them; the resolver hint text is pinned (ObjectResolverTests), and the live check is queued as VRF-019 step 22. This follows the project's stated route for host adapters (project-state `infrastructure_dependencies`), so it is not rated as untested behaviour. Default: ACCEPT, and treat step 22 as the evidence the release PR needs. Moving the text into a host-free helper with a test would buy a review round.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/ToolHelpers.cs"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T021638Z-269e1e06", "fid": "R-18"}, "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "R-18 and R-6: the change fragment still records the decisions these fixes changed", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `.prawduct/changes/canvas-read.md` was not touched by the fix commits. Its Decisions paragraph still says 'a GUID or prefix reaches any object' (the R-18 fix now refuses a group's id on every action that does not act on groups) and 'with `status` for the full list' (the R-6 fix says status lists components only), and its Consumer note does not carry the three Breaking entries the fixes added to CHANGELOG.md (move refuses a second position for one object; a group's id is refused where a group has no meaning; a repeated id in delete, preview or enable is one action). Smaller, same family: the CHANGELOG group-refusal bullet lists `tree` among the actions answering with the default text, but tree words its own ('\u2026 is a group; tree reads components and parameters'). The build plan does record the narrowing, so the decision itself is on the record. These are record edits in non-judgeable files: they move no coverage and can ride the disposition commit the plan's last box is waiting for. Note it in the build plan or `.prawduct/.handoff-notes.md` so that commit carries it.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/canvas-read.md", "CHANGELOG.md"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T021638Z-269e1e06", "fid": "R-18"}, "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "R-19: new VRF-019 step 22 needs a group after step 17 deletes the only one", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The four sites R-19 named are corrected and it is recorded fixed. The same fix added step 22 ('A group's GUID on gh_wire list, gh_inspect outputs and gh_canvas get is refused \u2026 while move and delete still act on the group') after step 17, which deletes POSTS, the only group on the stated canvas, and whose own text says it 'comes after every other step that needs it'. The operator has to create a group for step 22 without being told to. Move step 22 before step 17 or tell the operator to create a group first. `.prawduct/operator-verification.md` is non-judgeable, so this edit is free and can ride the disposition commit.", "files": [".prawduct/operator-verification.md"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T021638Z-269e1e06", "fid": "R-19"}, "oid": "O-7"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "canvas-read", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["05"], "chunks_proposed": ["05"], "chunk": "05", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-canvas-read.md", ".prawduct/operator-verification.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "README.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/BestPracticesGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/CanvasOutlineGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/CommonErrorsGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/DataTreesGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/GettingStartedGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/Prompts/OptimizeCanvas.md"], "chunk_graded": "05", "chunks_graded": ["05"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-canvas-read.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-10T02:47:09Z"}}
